{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_project_overview", "label": "Jana2u POS Project", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_npm_run_dev", "label": "npm run dev", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_npm_run_format", "label": "npm run format", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_npm_run_lint", "label": "npm run lint", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_npm_run_type_check", "label": "npm run type-check", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_npm_run_build", "label": "npm run build", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_npm_run_preview", "label": "npm run preview", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_post_change_verification_rule", "label": "Post-Change Verification Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Commands", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After every change, run npm run format && npm run lint && npm run type-check && npm run build and fix any errors before considering the work done, to keep the codebase consistently formatted, lint-clean, type-safe and buildable."}, {"id": "claude_responsive_mobile_ui", "label": "Responsive & Mobile UI Layout Tiers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app targets three layout tiers (mobile <768px one region, tablet 768-1199px two columns with tab-switch, desktop 1200px+ full multi-column) derived from Mantine 9 default breakpoints, so every new screen must be tested and shaped around these tiers rather than ad hoc widths."}, {"id": "claude_uselayouttier_hook", "label": "useLayoutTier() Hook", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_useismobile_hook", "label": "useIsMobile() Hook", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_layouttierprovider", "label": "LayoutTierProvider", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single shared media-query subscription mounted once above the router, instead of ~40 independent useMediaQuery listeners, so one breakpoint crossing does not fire a synchronized re-render burst across the whole tree that collides with in-flight CSS transitions. Uses getInitialValueInEffect:false to avoid a first-frame flash of the wrong layout."}, {"id": "claude_billingregions_component", "label": "BillingRegions.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_cartlineitem_component", "label": "CartLineItem.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_animation_performance_rules", "label": "Animation Performance Rules", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Animation performance", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Derived from a real incident: navigating into Billing appeared to make the left navbar 'shrink' with a stuck animation. Root cause was AppShell's own chrome transition (driven by isBillingPage) racing Billing's heavy first mount, worsened by an unrelated left-property animation and an app-wide re-render fan-out. Rules: only animate transform/opacity (compositor-only), snap route/screen boundaries instead of animating them, never call useMediaQuery directly, and never pair a @keyframes animation with transition: all on the same element."}, {"id": "claude_appshell_component", "label": "AppShell.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Animation performance / Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_isbillingboundarychange_pattern", "label": "isBillingBoundaryChange Render-Time State Adjustment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Animation performance", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Suppresses AppShell's Mantine transition for the one render where a billing-specific boundary (header height/navbar width/padding) is crossed, so an animated chrome resize doesn't land in the same frame as a heavy screen's first mount and appear stuck."}, {"id": "claude_amountinput_component", "label": "AmountInput.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Animation performance / Responsive & mobile UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_cartpanel_component", "label": "CartPanel.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Animation performance", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_catalogpanel_component", "label": "CatalogPanel.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Responsive & mobile UI / Animation performance", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_ui_copy_plain_language_rule", "label": "UI Copy \u2014 Plain Language Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "UI copy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app's user is a non-technical, possibly non-native-English-speaking shop owner, so all user-facing text must avoid standards names/internals (EAN-13, GS1, SKU collision rules, delta, cursor, outbox, idempotency), developer/DB jargon (immutable, validation error, vendor, intake), must plainly state optionality and repeatability, and validation messages must say what to do rather than what failed."}, {"id": "claude_productformmodal_component", "label": "ProductFormModal.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "UI copy / Center modals", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_center_modal_pattern", "label": "Center Modal Visual Family", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Center modals \u2014 one visual family", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every center-opening Modal follows ProductFormModal's pattern: plain-text no-icon title, no radius override (defaultRadius:'md' applies), centered + fullScreen={isMobile} except small confirm dialogs, standard footer (Cancel variant='default', primary action blue), uppercase section labels, and blue as the only brand accent (semantic colors like green/orange/red stay independent)."}, {"id": "claude_confirmdialog_component", "label": "ConfirmDialog.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Center modals \u2014 one visual family", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_a4invoicepreviewmodal_component", "label": "A4InvoicePreviewModal.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Center modals \u2014 one visual family / Keyboard shortcuts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_detail_drawer_pattern", "label": "Right-Side Detail Drawer Visual Family", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Right-side detail & profile drawers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every right-side entity detail drawer follows a standard shape: icon+title/subtitle header, hero identity card, 3-column metrics snapshot Grid, tabbed operations (Tabs.List grow), inline expandable Collapse actions, and a metadata + Delete/Close/Edit footer, so entity profile drawers look and behave consistently across features."}, {"id": "claude_producttable_component", "label": "ProductTable.tsx (Item Specifications Drawer)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Right-side detail & profile drawers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_supplierdetaildrawer_component", "label": "SupplierDetailDrawer.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Right-side detail & profile drawers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_employeedetaildrawer_component", "label": "EmployeeDetailDrawer.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Right-side detail & profile drawers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_useappshortcuts_hook", "label": "useAppShortcuts (Global Keyboard Shortcut Engine)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Keyboard shortcuts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_keyboardshortcutsmodal_component", "label": "KeyboardShortcutsModal.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Keyboard shortcuts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_entry_chain_architecture", "label": "App Entry Chain", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_router_tsx", "label": "src/app/router.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_feature_module_pattern", "label": "Feature Module Pattern (components/, types.ts, index.ts barrel)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each feature module (auth, billing, customers, inventory, print-jobs, repairs, reports) shares the same shape and is imported only through its barrel (@/features/billing), not by reaching into components/, to keep module boundaries enforced."}, {"id": "claude_path_alias", "label": "@/* Path Alias", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_apiclient", "label": "ApiClient (src/api/client.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture / Offline & sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_querykeys", "label": "src/api/queryKeys.ts Query Key Factory", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_constants_module", "label": "src/constants/ Shared Business Constants", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_redux_store", "label": "Redux Toolkit Store (src/store/)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "State management", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_cartslice", "label": "cartSlice.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "State management", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_themeslice_colorschememanager", "label": "themeSlice.ts + reduxColorSchemeManager", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "State management", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_syncslice", "label": "syncSlice.ts (Read-Only Mirror)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "State management", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_design_tokens_cssvariablesresolver", "label": "cssVariablesResolver.ts Design Tokens", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "State management / Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_money_handling_moneyts", "label": "money.ts (Integer-Cents Money Handling)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Money handling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_offline_sync_architecture", "label": "Offline & Sync Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Offline & sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The shop loses internet regularly (power cuts, ISP outages), so the app is offline-first: every synced resource mirrors into IndexedDB via Dexie and the UI reads only that mirror; writes apply locally first and queue in a durable outbox flushed on reconnect."}, {"id": "claude_dexie_schema", "label": "Dexie Schema (src/offline/db/schema.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Offline & sync / Local schema changes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_outbox_pattern", "label": "Durable Outbox Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Offline & sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writes apply locally first and queue in a durable outbox table that flushes when connectivity returns; the outbox, idMap, conflicts and stockLedger tables hold data that exists nowhere else and must be migrated in place, never dropped."}, {"id": "claude_syncresource_descriptor_pattern", "label": "SyncResource Descriptor Pattern", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Adding a module to sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_products_resource", "label": "products.resource.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Adding a module to sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_invoices_resource", "label": "invoices.resource.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Adding a module to sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checkout is one compound server-side write (invoice + payment + stock decrement + ticket-delivery + customer-balance update) whose non-invoice side effects can each independently fail into a warnings[] list; localApply writes only the invoice row and stock deltas, and push requests unscoped follow-up pulls for payments/repairs/printJobs/customers rather than optimistically mirroring them."}, {"id": "claude_stockledger", "label": "stockLedger.ts (Local Delta Ledger)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Offline & sync (Hard Rule 3)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never store an absolute value for anything that accumulates: stock is the server's baseline plus a local delta ledger, since deltas commute across devices but absolute overwrites do not (two terminals each selling one unit must produce -1 and -1, not conflicting totals)."}, {"id": "claude_localid_module", "label": "localId.ts (Provisional local_ IDs)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Offline & sync (Hard Rule 4)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never invent a server-generated identity locally: sku, barcodes and every key/id come from the server; rows created offline get a provisional local_<uuid> id and the engine rewrites every reference to it at flush time."}, {"id": "claude_connectivitymonitor", "label": "ConnectivityMonitor", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Connectivity", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "navigator.onLine alone is not a connectivity signal (it only sees the link layer), so ConnectivityMonitor combines it with the apiClient interceptor's statusCode:0 signal and a GET /health probe, with asymmetric hysteresis: offline publishes immediately, online is held for a settle window."}, {"id": "claude_sync_notifications", "label": "syncNotifications.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Notifications", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sync toasts use a stable notification id with notifications.update() and are edge-triggered with bookkeeping at module scope in SyncProvider, since the engine is a singleton whose effect re-runs on every auth flip and twice under StrictMode; 'Saved to the server' fires only when the change had actually been waiting so online edits don't bury the user in toasts."}, {"id": "claude_syncprovider", "label": "SyncProvider", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Notifications / State management", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_auth_offline_initializeauth", "label": "initializeAuth (Offline Auth Grace Period)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Auth while offline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Treats anything short of an outright 401/403 rejection as unverified rather than invalid: it restores the cached identity from Dexie and sets isOfflineSession with a 7-day grace period, since an unreachable server or a 500 from /auth/me doesn't mean the credentials went bad."}, {"id": "claude_authslice", "label": "authSlice (login/loginSuccess cacheSession)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Auth while offline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The session is cached on login as well as on a successful /auth/me; caching only in initializeAuth meant a cashier who logged in and then lost connectivity had nothing to restore from on the next reload."}, {"id": "claude_backend_sync_contract", "label": "Backend Sync Contract (Rust/Axum)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Backend contract", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every syncable collection soft-deletes (never hard-deletes) so a delta pull can see deletions; GET /sync/changes is one multiplexed delta endpoint so a reconnect is one round trip; GET /sync/status returns the cursor for the newest row since /sync/changes pages oldest-first; Idempotency-Key on every mutating request makes retrying a request whose response was lost to a power cut safe; If-Match/version gives 409 VERSION_CONFLICT; the server is the oversell authority via 409 INSUFFICIENT_STOCK."}, {"id": "claude_sequences_reserve_endpoint", "label": "POST /sequences/{name}/reserve", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Backend contract", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sequential human-facing numbers (INV-2026-0042, REP-\u2026, PRT-\u2026) are minted server-side at the moment a sale/repair/print-job is created, never client-side; a ticket created offline has no number until its create operation reaches the server."}, {"id": "claude_pwa_vite_plugin_pwa", "label": "vite-plugin-pwa Service Worker", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "PWA", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Precaches the app shell so a reload during an outage doesn't show the browser offline page; registerType:'prompt' (never autoUpdate) because an update reload would drop the active cart; no runtimeCaching for /api so a cached 200 doesn't make a dead backend look online."}, {"id": "claude_appupdateprompt_component", "label": "AppUpdatePrompt.tsx", "file_ty